{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the theorem of Narayanan, Vasudevan and Somasundaram (arXiv:2610.16258) that every finite elementary graph satisfies ch(G) = χ(G) = ω(G) (chromaticChoosable_of_isElementary; clique number at most k implies k-choosability for every colour type, choosable_of_isElementary), together with the structure theorem of Maffray and Reed (JCTB 75, 1999, Theorem 2, (i) ⇒ (iii)) that the proof starts from: every finite elementary graph is an augmentation of the line graph of a bipartite multigraph, given by an explicit edge representation (rep_of_isElementary; IsAugLineGraphRep: vertex v is the edge {a v, b v} of a bipartite multigraph; non-adjacent pairs sharing an end share exactly one end, which is a hub with at most two neighbours; no edge joins two hubs). The earlier statements for the representation class are kept (choosable_of_rep, chromaticChoosable_of_rep, isElementary_of_rep, rep_of_lineGraph, rep_of_cobipartite). The choosability proof follows the paper (Hall, the Deficiency Lemma, saturation, Proposition 3.7, Galvin; Kőnig avoided). The Maffray–Reed proof follows the paper's induction by compression of strong homogeneous pairs (growth procedure from an induced D, claims (1)–(2), A-components, Theorem 5), with every forbidden-subgraph step done as a parity argument on a fixed elementary colouring; Theorems 3–4 are replaced by a \"bend\" lemma, and two exposition gaps of the paper (p. 143 and Case 3 of claim (2)) are repaired. Galvin's theorem for bipartite multigraphs is imported as a lake dependency from PALOMAR-2026-10-18-000029 v2.",
